                        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">The absolute first-line treatment for CHF and resulting edema. They work by forcing the kidneys to excrete sodium and water, reducing blood volume and venous pressure.</p>
                        <strong class="text-sm text-slate-800">Limitations/Why a Port is needed:</strong>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">Diuretic resistance often occurs. In severe CHF, kidneys receive less blood flow and stop responding. Furthermore, diuretics do not physically clear the stagnant lymph proteins from the interstitium, leading to fibrotic tissue changes over time.</p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <!-- Tab Content 2 -->
                    <div id="tab-paracentesis" class="tab-content hidden">
