                        <p class="text-slate-600 mb-4">Experimental/novel surgical approaches. Connecting the thoracic duct to a lower-pressure vein (Lymphovenous bypass) or externally draining it.</p>
                        <strong class="text-sm text-slate-800">The Port-a-Cath Opportunity:</strong>
                        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">This is where your project lives. Current external drains are prone to infection and clotting. A subcutaneous Port-a-Cath accessing the thoracic duct would allow for intermittent, sterile, controlled decompression of the lymphatic system in refractory CHF patients without permanent open stomata.</p>
                    </div>
