                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Thoracic duct is 2-5mm, highly distensible, thin-walled (lacks strong muscularis layer).</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Catheter tip must be highly atraumatic, soft (silicone/polyurethane), to prevent vessel perforation. Fixation mechanisms must not occlude the fragile duct.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50">
                            <td class="py-3 px-4 font-medium text-slate-800">Hemodynamics</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">Near-zero pressure system. Forward flow dependent on valves and breathing.</td>
                            <td class="py-3 px-4">The port reservoir cannot rely on patient blood pressure to flush itself. High risk of backflow/stagnation. May require specialized anti-reflux valve in the catheter tip.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50">
